  "owned_code": "rederive3-owned-files.json",
  "notes": [
    "HistoricalPrivateRecoveryReconciliationAttested defaults false; source erasure refuses before any mutation without explicit store-wide owner attestation. Only known synthetic fixture inventories enable it.",
    "Discoverable PII-bearing live and ordinary/streamed rebuild preparations use SDK registration, closure, terminal fences and payload-free barriers. Guarded v3 replay keeps one SDK private manifest plus a content-free pointer; cold adapters verify current owner selection and terminal evidence after reclamation.",
    "Fixed recoverable empty-v1 initialization bytes/fingerprint are unchanged and independently resumed in two old-manifest controls. Existing v1/v2 generic owners retain their default policy.",
    "SDK owner-proof reading was factored unchanged into a shared serialized-state reader so the testing adapter exercises the same current-owner checks as Dapr.",
    "The original full source/query lane (889), full native lane (81), Client package (340), OCI/publisher/CI proofs remain preserved; final corrections were followed by the affected source (148), SDK (2156), dispatcher (66), replay (3), native class (24), and package lanes.",
    "Cold guarded controls serialize all physical bytes and import them into a new SDK adapter between preparation, commit, verification, erasure and stale replay.",
    "Source/package/catalog selections and constructor signatures are unchanged. No production attestation, migration/deletion, deployment or release dispatch was executed.",
    "Parent/user owner publication advanced EventStore to fd083a91b and Memories to d9826761 during implementation. Child made no Git mutations; final task-owned raw and LF-normalized code hashes are independent of those moving heads.",
    "Known prior broad workspace blockers and pre-existing skipped controls remain explicit; focused results do not certify matching package publication."
  ]
